if __name__=='__main__':
 upstream=read('upstream.json');hist=by_project('history.json');sizes=by_project('sizes.json');build=by_project('build-at-t.json');verify=read('verification.json')
 lines=['# Commit-survival project survey','','Every table value is rendered by `python3 docker/stage0_handover.py` from the measured JSON artifacts. Measurement invocations: `python3 docker/stage0_upstream.py` (repository/HEAD); `python3 docker/stage0_match_snapshot.py` (snapshot); `python3 docker/stage0_history.py` (history/tags); `python3 docker/stage0_count_methods.py` (annotations/methods); from docker/, `docker compose run --rm ktester bash -c \'python /work/docker/stage0_build_tests.py\'` (builds/tests); `python3 docker/stage0_verify.py` (independent matches and off-line release probes). Exact per-project commands and environments are in the corresponding reports and JSON.','','t is an exact or best normalized source match on the default first-parent line. This is a survey anchor, not proof of the authors’ original checkout. Δ lists changed/snapshot-only/commit-only files. Tags in the main table point directly to that line and before includes t. Date is the committer date. Test totals include skipped tests and, for Gson, all reactor modules. Blank executed-test cells mean no run/evidence. No project is selected.','','| Project | Upstream repo | Snapshot match (SHA, date, exact or Δ) | Nearest tag before / after | First-parent commits after t | Change src/main | Release tags after t | Dev @Test at t | Dev tests executed | Non-private methods | Build at t (JDK) | Dev test wall seconds | Notes |','|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---|']
